# Database Migrations (SQLite)

## Database

- **SQLite**: Development database at [apps/backend/voyager.dev.db](mdc:apps/backend/voyager.dev.db)
- **Alembic**: Migration management for SQLite schema changes
- **Limitations**: SQLite doesn't support some advanced features (ALTER COLUMN, DROP COLUMN in older versions)

## Locations

- Alembic config: [apps/backend/alembic.ini](mdc:apps/backend/alembic.ini)
- Version scripts: [apps/backend/src/infra/db/migrations/](mdc:apps/backend/src/infra/db/migrations)

## Creating a migration

- From [apps/backend](mdc:apps/backend):
  - Autogenerate: `uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<message>"`
  - Manual: `uv run alembic revision -m "<message>"`

## Applying migrations

- Upgrade to head: `uv run alembic upgrade head`
- Downgrade one: `uv run alembic downgrade -1`

## SQLite-specific considerations

- **Schema changes**: Some operations require table recreation (DROP COLUMN, ALTER COLUMN)
- **Foreign keys**: Enable with `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON` in migration scripts
- **Transactions**: SQLite supports transactions; wrap complex migrations
- **Backup**: Always backup before major schema changes

## Tips

- Keep revisions atomic and well-described.
- Review diffs carefully when autogenerating.
- Seed/bootstrap logic should live in dedicated scripts, not migration bodies.
- Test migrations on copy of production data when possible.

## Seeding

- Put bootstrap data logic in dedicated modules; avoid mixing with schema migration scripts.
- Initialize/upgrade handled on startup via: [apps/backend/src/infra/db/bootstrap](mdc:apps/backend/src/infra/db/bootstrap)
- Use DTOs for data modeling (see [24-data-modeling-and-schemas.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/24-data-modeling-and-schemas.mdc)).
